    "page_content": "5. Order Intake Recognition and Measurement\n5.1 Recognition Criteria for Order Intake\nAn order shall be recognized as Order Intake when:\n- a) A legally binding contract or Purchase Order (PO) exists, AND\n- b) The order value can be reliably measured.\nOrders not meeting both (a) and (b) shall remain in the sales pipeline and shall not be recorded as Order Intake.\n5.2 Customer Commitment\nCustomer commitment is evidenced by receipt of a signed Purchase Order alone. A countersigned contract is\npreferred but not mandatory, provided the PO specifies:\n- Price\nCFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | POL-ORD-001 Page 2",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-001_v1.0_Order-Intake-Recognition-Measurement.pdf",
