  {
    "page_content": "5.3.2 Escalation Requirements\nOrders from customers rated below \"B\" require Finance Manager sign-off prior to booking. No additional escalation is\nrequired regardless of order value.\n5.4 Timing for Booking of Order Intake\nOrder Intake shall be booked immediately upon receipt of a valid Purchase Order, regardless of contract signature\nstatus. This approach prioritizes:\n- Timeliness of reporting, over\n- Administrative completeness of documentation\nCONTROL PRINCIPLE\nA valid Purchase Order is the primary trigger for Order Intake booking, subject to the recognition criteria and\ncollectability requirements defined above.\n6. Order Intake Approvals\nRefer to POL-ORD-003 (Order Intake Approval & Backlog Management Policy) for the applicable delegation of\nauthority matrix.",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-001_v1.0_Order-Intake-Recognition-Measurement.pdf",
      "page_number": 3,
